project:
  name: meiyume_ai_assistant
  language: python
  description: >
    A comprehensive full-stack application with a Streamlit frontend and a Django backend for multiple 
    AI-powered assistants. The system currently supports CAD analysis and is designed to easily accommodate 
    additional AI assistants through a modular architecture. Each assistant can connect to different n8n workflows.

rules:
  - description: >
      The frontend is built with Streamlit and supports multiple AI assistants through a unified interface.
      Users can switch between different assistants (CAD, Quality, Complaint) via a sidebar selector.
  - description: >
      Django handles user authentication, upload logging, file storage, and metadata management across all assistants.
      It forwards uploaded files and metadata to appropriate n8n webhook endpoints based on the assistant type.
  - description: >
      The backend uses a modular architecture with a core module (meiyume_core) for shared functionality
      and individual assistant modules (assistants/cad, assistants/quality, assistants/complaint) for specific features.
  - description: >
      n8n is configured to receive HTTP POST requests for different assistants. Each assistant can have its own
      workflow configuration and can trigger different AI models (Google Gemini, OpenAI, etc.) based on the task.
  - description: >
      Include prompt-tuning logic in the n8n nodes before calling AI models, to improve result accuracy 
      on complex engineering, quality, or complaint analysis tasks.
  - description: >
      n8n responds with structured data or downloadable files, which Django stores and Streamlit presents to the user.
      Each assistant can have different output formats (CSV, reports, visualizations).
  - description: >
      Use Django REST Framework for building the API endpoints with assistant-specific routes (/api/cad/, /api/quality/, etc.)
      and Celery for managing asynchronous processing if needed in future versions.
  - description: >
      The backend uses PostgreSQL as the primary database, configured via Django's settings.
      It stores user data, file uploads, metadata, and links to processed results across all assistants.
  - description: >
      Django is integrated with Microsoft Azure Active Directory. All users log in using 
      their company Microsoft credentials via OAuth2 (Azure AD SSO).
  - description: >
      The system uses JWT (JSON Web Token) authentication for all API endpoints. JWT tokens are issued at /api/token/ and must be included as Bearer tokens in the Authorization header for all protected endpoints. Token refresh and verification endpoints are provided at /api/token/refresh/ and /api/token/verify/.
  - description: >
      JWT settings: 24h access token, 7d refresh token, rotation and blacklisting enabled, HS256 algorithm, secret key from environment. All API endpoints require authentication unless explicitly marked as public.
  - description: >
      The system is designed for easy extensibility. Adding a new assistant requires:
      1. Creating a new assistant module under backend/assistants/
      2. Defining assistant-specific models, views, and serializers
      3. Creating corresponding n8n workflow
      4. Adding frontend interface in Streamlit
      5. Updating URL routing and admin configuration

